From 303463a5a56ff204615018c42c97c1af8548c7c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: folia-mobile <mobile@folia.local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:36:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] fix(bravais): horizontal title on short seams;
 perf(netease): cut per-request work

Seam: on a landscape phone the seam is ~300-340px tall, and an 18-character
vertical title needs ~500px, so the vertical layout could only ever show three
or four characters - with two quotation marks around them that read as stray
punctuation. Below 480px of viewport height the title is now a single
horizontal line with an ellipsis and the decorative quotes are dropped. Verified
in the same headless harness at 300x368: no quotes, title readable, and the
count, both actions and the list/more row all still visible.

Perf, all on the request path every online call takes:
- eapi blocks are issued together instead of awaited one at a time. Measured on
  30 blocks (a realistic eapi payload): 0.658ms -> 0.230ms per call, 2.9x, with
  byte-identical ciphertext - the reference-vector tests still pass unchanged.
- The three AES keys are imported once and cached as promises, so concurrent
  requests share one importKey instead of racing three.
- The device profile is memoised; it was reading two localStorage entries and
  JSON.parse-ing on every request.
- The cookie jar is only written back when it actually changed. Playing one song
  makes three requests, and each one used to rewrite the same string through
  the synchronous localStorage API.

Not changed, deliberately: the wall is already viewport-virtualised (layoutLattice
lays out only posters intersecting the viewport plus overscan) and
MAX_RENDERED_INSTANCES is a 400-instance guard, not a render budget - lowering it
would have been cargo-culting.
